  "deviations": [
    "Section 5 test vector uses mean return as the performance metric R rather than Sharpe, which the paper allows via metric pluggability; chosen so every ranking and λ is hand-exact with no std-dev edge cases.",
    "Paper body prints binom(16,8)=12,780; note records the correct binomial 12,870 and flags the discrepancy."
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "v0.1 code will need an explicit convention for metric ties and argmax index ties; paper examples assume unique rankings.",
    "Exact Sharpe definition (excess return, ddof, annualization) left to the implementation ticket when metric=R Sharpe is wired."
  ],
  "notes_for_referee": "Primary algorithm map is Alg. 2.3 / Def. 2.2 / §3.1 in the Feb 2015 author PDF. Recompute §5 combinations 1–6 from the integer matrix; expected logits {0, ln(1/3), 0, 0, ln(1/3), ln(1/3)} and PBO=0.5. Only docs/research/pbo-cscv.md was added."
